---
---

<section class="scene scene-building" id="building" style="flex-direction: column; min-height: 130vh;">
  <div class="legend-card left" style="top: 15%;">
    <div class="legend-portrait legend-portrait-archival">
      <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2a/George_Washington_Carver_c1910.jpg" alt="George Washington Carver" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="legend-info">
      <div class="legend-name">George Washington Carver</div>
      <div class="legend-years">1864 &ndash; 1943</div>
      <div class="legend-desc">Agricultural scientist. 300+ products from peanuts. Revolutionized Southern farming.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="legend-card right" style="top: 45%;">
    <div class="legend-portrait legend-portrait-archival">
      <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Garrett_Morgan.jpg" alt="Garrett Morgan" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="legend-info">
      <div class="legend-name">Garrett Morgan</div>
      <div class="legend-years">1877 &ndash; 1963</div>
      <div class="legend-desc">Invented the traffic signal and gas mask. Saved lives with innovations he was rarely credited for.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="legend-card left" style="top: 75%;">
    <div class="legend-portrait legend-portrait-transitional">
      <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/62/Katherine_Johnson_at_NASA%2C_in_1966.jpg" alt="Katherine Johnson at NASA" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="legend-info">
      <div class="legend-name">Katherine Johnson</div>
      <div class="legend-years">1918 &ndash; 2020</div>
      <div class="legend-desc">NASA mathematician. Calculated orbital trajectory for John Glenn. Hidden figure, towering legacy.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="max-width: 900px; width: 100%; position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div class="scene-divider reveal" style="margin-bottom: 40px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #D4A843, #55ac64);"></div>
    <p class="reveal font-display" style="font-size: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px); font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 56px; line-height: 1.4;">
      From freedom, they didn't just survive.<br /><span style="color: #D4A843; font-weight: 600;">They built.</span>
    </p>

    <div class="reveal from-left" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <figure class="scene-image img-archival" style="margin: 0;">
        <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fa/Tuskegee_Institute_in_1882.jpg" alt="Tuskegee Institute, 1882" loading="lazy" style="border-radius: 12px; width: 100%; max-height: 280px; object-fit: cover;" />
        <figcaption>Tuskegee Institute, 1882. Public domain.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div style="padding: 16px 0;">
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 3px; color: rgba(212, 168, 67, 0.5); margin-bottom: 8px;">1881</p>
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Tuskegee Institute</p>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6); line-height: 1.7;">Booker T. Washington builds an institution from nothing. HBCUs become launchpads for Black excellence.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal from-right" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <div style="padding: 16px 0;">
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 3px; color: rgba(85, 172, 100, 0.5); margin-bottom: 8px;">1921</p>
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Black Wall Street</p>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6); line-height: 1.7;">Greenwood, Tulsa. Black commerce thriving &mdash; until it was burned to the ground. They rebuilt.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="scene-image img-archival" style="margin: 0;">
        <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/be/Tulsa-1921-booker.jpg" alt="Tulsa, 1921" loading="lazy" style="border-radius: 12px; width: 100%; max-height: 280px; object-fit: cover;" />
        <figcaption>Tulsa, 1921. Public domain.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal scale-in" style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <figure class="scene-image-full img-transitional img-fade-edges">
        <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/1963_march_on_washington.jpg" alt="March on Washington, August 28, 1963" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 16px;">
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 3px; color: rgba(200, 67, 66, 0.5); margin-bottom: 8px;">1964</p>
        <p class="font-display" style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Civil Rights Act</p>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6); line-height: 1.7;">After centuries of being denied, the law finally said: every table is your table.</p>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55); margin-top: 10px; font-style: italic;">March on Washington, August 28, 1963. Public domain.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="reveal font-display" style="font-size: clamp(16px, 2.5vw, 22px); font-weight: 400; opacity: 0.6; text-align: center; line-height: 1.6;">
      Every generation built. Every generation was told it wasn't enough.<br />
      <span style="color: #D4A843;">So we kept building.</span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
